From: Filipe Manana <fdmanana@suse.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:43:41 +0100
Subject: btrfs: abort transaction on failure to update inode for hole punching
 and reflinking
Git-commit: 97fcd34aa9fd73cefe3120ac9a82ca9d7763922f
Patch-mainline: v7.3-rc4
References: CVE-2026-98269 bsc#1284606

If we fail to update the inode we error out without aborting the
transaction, which can result in a persistent inconsistency if after
the failure the transaction is committed, as we have dropped file
extent items from a range and either punched a hole or insert a new file
extent item for that range (for reflinks).

So add the missing transaction abort.

Fixes: 2aaa66558172 ("Btrfs: add hole punching")
Reviewed-by: Qu Wenruo <wqu@suse.com>
Signed-off-by: Filipe Manana <fdmanana@suse.com>
Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
Acked-by: Daniel Vacek <neelx@suse.com>
---
 fs/btrfs/file.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/btrfs/file.c b/fs/btrfs/file.c
index 20e15dc30bfb5..f978c6524aa03 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/file.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/file.c
@@ -2564,8 +2564,10 @@ int btrfs_replace_file_extents(struct btrfs_inode *inode,
 		}
 
 		ret = btrfs_update_inode(trans, root, inode);
-		if (ret)
+		if (unlikely(ret)) {
+			btrfs_abort_transaction(trans, ret);
 			break;
+		}
 
 		btrfs_end_transaction(trans);
 		btrfs_btree_balance_dirty(fs_info);

